WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:04.310
So A, we've been talking over the last several
weeks about just like the total havoc that's

00:00:04.310 --> 00:00:07.911
been, uh, happening on the David Pakman show
youtube channel.

00:00:07.911 --> 00:00:12.890
And we had the really great news earlier this
week of reaching 700,000 youtube subscribers.

00:00:12.890 --> 00:00:18.810
I think we're now closer to 704,000 maybe
705.

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:23.130
And to catch you up there have sort of been
three primary issues that we're facing on

00:00:23.130 --> 00:00:25.350
the youtube channel, which is just one of
our outlets, right?

00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:27.740
We're on 200 radio and TV stations.

00:00:27.740 --> 00:00:30.480
We've got an audio podcast that has been growing
significantly.

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:35.890
It has grown 40% since my appearance on the
Joe Rogan program, interestingly enough, and

00:00:35.890 --> 00:00:37.230
that's been really great.

00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:41.630
We've got the free speech TV broadcast of
the show on Directv and dish network and then

00:00:41.630 --> 00:00:44.130
we've got youtube, which is a big piece of
what we do.

00:00:44.130 --> 00:00:50.239
The three issues we've been been dealing with
are deep prioritization in youtube algorithm

00:00:50.239 --> 00:00:51.920
in favor of corporate media.

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:56.650
What I mean by that is when you watch a video
on youtube, youtube recommends additional

00:00:56.650 --> 00:01:00.539
videos to you and as I've detailed extensively,
I won't do it again today.

00:01:00.539 --> 00:01:01.550
Don't worry.

00:01:01.550 --> 00:01:07.259
Um, youtube has been increasingly suggesting
people watch corporate youtube channels like

00:01:07.259 --> 00:01:12.680
CNN, MSNBC, the late night shows, produced
with, you know, tens or hundreds of millions

00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:14.700
of dollars behind them, et cetera.

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:17.149
Rather than independent content like ours.

00:01:17.149 --> 00:01:21.159
We've lost about 3 million views a month as
a result of that algorithmic change.

00:01:21.159 --> 00:01:26.000
The other issue has been demonetization of
videos that should be earning money.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:29.740
They don't violate any of youtube monetization
rules as they are written.

00:01:29.740 --> 00:01:33.009
Although the devil seems to be in the interpretation
of those rules.

00:01:33.009 --> 00:01:37.821
We will produce a video, research it, edit,
upload, all of that stuff and then a youtube

00:01:37.821 --> 00:01:40.789
algorithm will determine it's not going to
run any ads.

00:01:40.789 --> 00:01:45.259
Sorry, you don't get to make any money off
of this content you've spent all day creating

00:01:45.259 --> 00:01:49.310
a, that's been issue number two and issue
number three, which is the one I've spoken

00:01:49.310 --> 00:01:53.609
the least about is people reporting to me
that they have been subscribed for a long

00:01:53.609 --> 00:01:57.569
time in many cases and then all of a sudden
they notice they're not seeing our videos

00:01:57.569 --> 00:01:58.819
on their homepage anymore.

00:01:58.819 --> 00:02:04.130
They specifically go to our channel and all
of a sudden they realize they're not even

00:02:04.130 --> 00:02:05.130
subscribed.

00:02:05.130 --> 00:02:06.710
We have not talked that much about it.

00:02:06.710 --> 00:02:08.899
I have been telling you tube for months.

00:02:08.899 --> 00:02:14.909
Every time I have a call with our youtube,
uh, rep, I say, or almost every time we are

00:02:14.909 --> 00:02:20.079
continuing to get dozens of emails from people
who say, I'm, I'm not incompetent.

00:02:20.079 --> 00:02:22.510
I know I was subscribed to your channel.

00:02:22.510 --> 00:02:23.939
I am now unsubscribed.

00:02:23.939 --> 00:02:31.540
And, uh, one of the unfortunate things is
that we just hit 700,000 subscribers who knows

00:02:31.540 --> 00:02:35.420
where we would be, where this unsubscription
problem, not an issue.

00:02:35.420 --> 00:02:40.129
And I finally got a video from a viewer of
this happening and you will notice that the

00:02:40.129 --> 00:02:45.659
viewer, this is on Youtube Mobile app, uh,
similar activity has been told to me is taking

00:02:45.659 --> 00:02:50.510
place on desktop of viewer, sent me a video
from mobile and you see him click onto our

00:02:50.510 --> 00:02:51.510
channel.

00:02:51.510 --> 00:02:56.000
And even though he thought he was subscribed,
he wasn't, he clicks the subscribe button,

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:57.220
it seems to work.

00:02:57.220 --> 00:03:02.740
And as soon as he comes right back to our
channel, he has again been unsubscribed.

00:03:02.740 --> 00:03:09.439
So this is only part one, like this is the
issue of subscribe isn't sticking and he immediately

00:03:09.439 --> 00:03:10.439
noticed it.

00:03:10.439 --> 00:03:15.280
The bigger issue might be people who have
been subscribed for a long time, they are

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:16.560
subscribed to a bunch of channels.

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:19.569
So they don't necessarily immediately notice
that they're not seeing our videos and their

00:03:19.569 --> 00:03:20.890
subscription feed.

00:03:20.890 --> 00:03:25.639
They come back to our channel when they think
about it and they realize, oh, I've been unsubscribed

00:03:25.639 --> 00:03:28.930
from the David Pakman show and this has a
cumulative effect.

00:03:28.930 --> 00:03:33.940
What I mean by that is subscriber growth creates
subscriber growth.

00:03:33.940 --> 00:03:38.769
If you have a hundred people who are subscribed
and sharing your content, now everyone who

00:03:38.769 --> 00:03:44.310
sees those hundred people's social media posts
about our content are more likely to become

00:03:44.310 --> 00:03:46.090
subscribers themselves.

00:03:46.090 --> 00:03:50.519
They are then likely to generate more subscribers
for us, so the value of one subscriber has

00:03:50.519 --> 00:03:54.400
a sort of economic multiplier effect to use
an economic term.

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:59.680
If there are a thousand people unsubscribed,
that means there are a thousand of fewer people

00:03:59.680 --> 00:04:05.530
sharing our content from which we would derive
even more subscribers in the future.

00:04:05.530 --> 00:04:07.099
So this is depressing.

00:04:07.099 --> 00:04:08.400
It's disappointing.

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:09.620
I can do nothing about it.

00:04:09.620 --> 00:04:12.249
I've told Youtube about it probably 20 times.

00:04:12.249 --> 00:04:16.880
If you have other videos like the one we showed
or other information, if you're noticing it's

00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:20.950
happening in particular browsers, if you're
noticing it's happening on mobile and not

00:04:20.950 --> 00:04:22.919
desktop or vice versa.

00:04:22.919 --> 00:04:24.539
Any information you have, please get to me.

00:04:24.539 --> 00:04:27.360
I don't have any reason to think right now
that this is malicious.

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:29.080
A lot of people report this.

00:04:29.080 --> 00:04:34.020
I think it's a glitch that youtube simply
hasn't fixed because even though many people

00:04:34.020 --> 00:04:39.530
tell them about it, rarely do we have examples
like this on video.

00:04:39.530 --> 00:04:40.530
Now we have one.

00:04:40.530 --> 00:04:42.602
Okay, so let me know if you have any more
light to shed on this problem.

